      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, and welcome. I'm Dr. [Name], a psychiatrist. Thank you for coming in today. What brings you to see me?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S014",
      "patient_response": "Well, hello Doctor. Thank you. I suppose I'm here because I just feel like I’m always up and moving around. Even on a quiet day when I'm supposed to be relaxing, I’m bouncing from writing out the garden club list to digging through my knitting bag, and then over to looking at travel papers before I’ve really finished any one of those things. \n\nSpeaking of travel, my sister is trying to get me to visit her in Arizona this winter. Have you ever been to Sedona? The red rocks are supposed to be just beautiful, but I don't know about flying these days. The airports are such a terrible mess. Last time I flew, they lost my checked bag for three whole days, and I had to buy all new toiletries at this tiny little pharmacy near the hotel. The pharmacist there was so sweet, though, she actually reminded me of my niece Sarah. Sarah just had her second baby, a little boy... wait, what did you ask me? Oh, right, why I'm here. Yes, I just always seem to be on the go and can't just settle down, I guess.",
